{
  "id": "29802_kasu",
  "headword": "{化|か}す",
  "reading": "かす",
  "romaji": "kasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to turn into; to change into; to become",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to turn into; to be transformed into",
      "explanation": "For something to change into a different state or thing, often a dramatic or unwelcome one. A literary variant of {化|か}する; the new state is marked with と or に."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29802_kasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{町|まち}が{廃墟|はいきょ}と{化|か}す。",
      "english": "The town turns into ruins.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29802_kasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{規則|きそく}が{形式|けいしき}だけのものと{化|か}してしまった。",
      "english": "The rule has turned into a mere formality.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29802_kasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{災害|さいがい}で{美|うつく}しい{景色|けしき}が{一面|いちめん}の{焼|や}け{野原|のはら}と{化|か}した。",
      "english": "In the disaster, the beautiful scenery turned into a scorched wasteland as far as the eye could see.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. The resulting state is marked with と (or に): Xと{化|か}す. A literary, written-style variant of {化|か}する with the same meaning; it often conveys a striking or unwelcome transformation.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Frequently used with negative outcomes: {廃墟|はいきょ}と{化|か}す (turn into ruins), {無|む}と{化|か}す (come to nothing).\n- The past form {化|か}した and the て form {化|か}して are the most common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {廃墟|はいきょ}と{化|か}す: to turn into ruins\n- {灰|はい}と{化|か}す: to be reduced to ashes",
